 "_doc": "Tabard equipment. Every item says which LAYERS it uses: paint = the outfit painting whose boxes it paints for its slot (data/outfits.json id; the boxes come from data/regions.json slots); geosets = swap-in mesh pieces it turns on; hides = pieces it forces off (a robe hides boot cuffs); attach = a separate model on a bone (data/props.json id). js/tabard.js reads this file only. Names are what a player sees. hidesHair: a head item that hides whatever the hair slot wears. fal: a fal.ai weapon or shield (avatar-3d/fal/data/catalog.json id) held on the Tabard grips; every held fal item is also offered automatically as 'fal:<id>' (js/tabard.js loadTabardData), so new fal weapons need no entry here.",
